// fuse_reg_group_selfT_fixed -- F2 (DESIGN.md 2.12.4), 7c regression: a fixed-size 2 x 2 target read transposed in
// its own update (`F = F.T * 1.0`), followed by `let g = F + 1.0`. The transpose of [1, 2; 3, 4] is [1, 3; 2, 4],
// so F[0,1] = 3, F[1,0] = 2, and g[0,1] = 4; an in-place fused loop would read already overwritten elements.
var F = [1.0, 2.0; 3.0, 4.0]
F = F.T * 1.0
let g = F + 1.0
printf("%.17g %.17g %.17g\n", F[0, 1], F[1, 0], g[0, 1])
